L wrote:
>>Rubbing non rusty armour could polish it, giving a 5% chance of
>>reflection, once only.
> 
> 
> Ahem! Reflection is a strictly magical effect which makes such diverse
> attacks as geysers of acid and spurts of sleeping gas to bounce off
> you, provided they are expressed in "ray" form. 

The rays can bounce off walls. Are they all enchanted?

Nethack isn't entirely logical, but it does have a lot of unexpected
interactions. Being able to polish up your armour would fit, provided
it was of sufficiently marginal usefulness not to unbalance the game.

> 
>>Rubbing blessed wooden items could be good luck, though there'd
>>have to be some counterbalance. Naturally, rubbing any cursed
>>item would be unlucky. 
> 
>  
> Mmm, too obscure.
> 

Obscure? Touching wood is one of the commonest superstitions,
and it makes sense it would matter if the wood were blessed
or cursed.

Nor is it obscure within the context of the game, not compared
to some of the other features in it.

